      en: "Balashikha, nestled in the extensive forested areas immediately east of the Russian capital, is the most populous metropolis in Moscow Oblast. The city, which emerged in the 19th century around prospering textile manufactories, has transformed in recent decades from a classic industrial center into one of Moscow's most dynamic suburbs. Although it is heavily integrated into the economic orbit of the capital today, Balashikha has retained an independent identity, which is primarily shaped by its historical importance as an armaments and military location, as well as by beautiful old manor houses like Pekhra-Yakovlevskoye. The surrounding lakes and extensive pine forests also offer a valuable recreation area in the otherwise densely populated Moscow agglomeration.",
