      en: ["Syktyvkar was officially known as Ust-Sysolsk until 1930.", "The city was first mentioned in historical records in 1586.", "Syktyvkar is home to one of the largest paper mills in Russia (Mondi).", "The average annual temperature in the city is a mere +1.3 °C.", "The city is home to Syktyvkar State University, which was founded in 1972.", "The local National Museum features artifacts of the 'Permian Animal Style' art."],
      es: ["Fundada en 1780 como Ust-Sysolsk", "Derechos de ciudad en 1780", "Población: unos 245.000 (2021)", "Aeropuerto de Syktyvkar (IATA: SCW) inaugurado en 1930", "La fábrica de papel Mondi Syktyvkar produce 700.000 toneladas anuales", "Universidad de Komi fundada en 1972"],
      pt: ["Fundada em 1780 como Ust-Sysolsk", "Direitos de cidade em 1780", "População: cerca de 245.000 (2021)", "Aeroporto de Syktyvkar (IATA: SCW) inaugurado em 1930", "A fábrica de papel Mondi Syktyvkar produz 700.000 toneladas anualmente", "Universidade de Komi fundada em 1972"],
