      en: ["Founded in 1830, it was known as Ulala until 1932.", "Awarded city status in 1928 during the Soviet administrative reforms.", "Current population is approximately 65,000 residents.", "The city's airport was modernized in 2011 to handle larger aircraft.", "Home to the Gorno-Altaysk State University, founded in 1949.", "The surrounding mountains reach heights of up to 400-600 meters."],
